{#
    A table, in the box that scrolls for it.

    The scroller has to be a box **around** the table. `overflow-x` on the
    `<table>` itself needs `display: block` to take effect, and that takes the
    element out of table layout: the row groups left inside generate an
    anonymous table box of their own, and that box shrink-wraps. The rule
    meant to rescue a table too wide for its column then quietly narrowed
    every table that was not too wide — a four-column reference sitting in the
    left third of the page with nothing beside it.

    Wrapped, nothing about the table changes. It stays a table, fills the
    column `document.css` gives it, and overflows the box only where its own
    minimum is wider than the column.

    The rest is the core's, included rather than copied: the class list, the
    inline widths a `:widths:` option sets, and the four parts.
#}
<div class="sds-table-scroll">
    <table {%- include "body/table/table-classes.html.twig" -%}
            {%- include "body/table/table-inline-style.html.twig" -%}>
        {% include "body/table/table-caption.html.twig" %}
        {% include "body/table/table-colgroups.html.twig" %}
        {% include "body/table/table-header.html.twig" %}
        {% include "body/table/table-body.html.twig" %}
    </table>
</div>
